r docstrings that obscure current behavior with repetition, obvious narration, duplicated explanation, or historical detail. The audit is pinned to `9e65567b79ffe872534c3c656ade7b34340d8192`.\n\n## Approach\nEdit explanatory text only in this directory/subsystem cohort. Condense it to current, non-obvious rationale and constraints; retain every file-specific preserve item and consumer contract below. Grouping adjacent files from one subsystem keeps the change reviewable in one session and permits one coherent verification pass without changing executable behavior.\n\n## Scope\n- `scripts/alert_dedup.py:2–22, 83–89, 96` — Preserve per-tag dedup, 24-hour cap, fail-soft behavior, JS-safe timestamp coercion. Consumer: none found.\n- `scripts/amend_commit_message.py:2–42, 153–156` — Preserve Change-Id/DCO carry-forward, refusal without Change-Id, hooks remain enabled. Consumer: none; argparse has separate concise text.\n- `scripts/backfill_caused_by.py:1–19, 64–70` — Preserve conservative resolver, dry-run default, closed-source write seam, derived provenance, idempotency. Consumer: full module docstring is argparse `--help`.\n- `scripts/backtest_bugfix_size.py:2–50, 84–87, 206–207, 269–279` — Preserve modes, pinned corpus identity, shipped predicates, offline inputs, usage. Consumer: full argparse `--help`.\n- `scripts/build_cloud_adf_corpus.py:2–27, 55–60` — Preserve deterministic sharded sample, scrubbing, frozen-update policy, paths. Consumer: full argparse `--help`.\n- `scripts/build_dc_wiki_corpus.py:2–29, 60–64` — Preserve stratification, scrubbing, frozen-update policy, paths. Consumer: full argparse `--help`.\n- `scripts/canary_bridge.py:1–11, 27–34, 73–75` — Preserve subcommand scope, invocation-independent sibling import, shared alert contract. Consumer: none found.\n- `scripts/capture_jira_fixtures.py:2–36, 47–60, 65–81` — Preserve exact response shapes, two redaction layers, opt-in/read-only behavior, comment cap. Consumer: full argparse `--help`.\n- `scripts/check_cli_json_js_safe.py:2–46, 71–74, 146–155` — Preserve JS-safe integer rule, sinks/roots, sanction, fail-closed and syntactic limitation. Consumer: full argparse `--help`.\n- `scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py:2–22, 54–56, 88–93` — Preserve triggers, durable acceptors, structural exclusion, path-context distinction. Consumer: full argparse `--help`.\n- `scripts/check_commit_message_wrap.py:2–27, 39–44, 49–62, 67–70` — Preserve 50/72 limits, exact exemptions, usage. Consumer: full argparse `--help`.\n- `scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py:2–72, 525–538, 549–550, 597–600` — Preserve threshold source, ratchet/counter semantics, exit/update rules, merge-base fail-closed fallback. Consumer: full argparse `--help`.\n- `scripts/check_config_ownership.py:49–52, 57–59` — Preserve which companion modules are composition roots. Consumer: none found.\n- `scripts/check_config_reads.py:2–32, 53–58, 447–456` — Preserve receiver-aware resolution strategies and ticket-pointer reporting behavior. Consumer: none found.\n- `scripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py:24–29, 68–82` — Preserve git-owned scope, fail-closed authored text, sanitized/capped diagnostics. Consumer: none found.\n- `scripts/check_deploy_manifest.py:2–40` — Preserve derivation sources, reasoned exclusions, coverage semantics, zero-path liveness floor. Consumer: none found.\n- `scripts/check_destructive_test_exec.py:2–29` — Preserve unsafe deletion shape, accepted guard/seam forms, static-analysis limit, safety rationale. Consumer: full argparse `--help`.\n- `scripts/check_fcntl_import_guard.py:2–41` — Preserve collection contract, flagged/allowed shapes, reasoned sanction. Consumer: full argparse `--help`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every listed location contains only current, non-obvious rationale or constraints after remediation; verified by reviewing the final diff against every Scope row.\n- [ ] Every preserve item and consumer contract in Scope remains explicit and accurate; verified by a row-by-row completion comment and the commands under Verification.\n- [ ] No executable behavior or test assertion changes; verified by the commands under Verification exiting 0.\n\n## Verification\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py`\n\nThe row-by-row diff review is authoritative for prose quality; the hygiene guard detects only its narrow deterministic history-token rule.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"scripts/alert_dedup.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"scripts/amend_commit_message.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"scripts/backfill_caused_by.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"scripts/backtest_bugfix_size.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"scripts/build_cloud_adf_corpus.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"scripts/build_dc_wiki_corpus.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"scripts/canary_bridge.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"scripts/capture_jira_fixtures.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"scripts/check_cli_json_js_safe.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"scripts/check_commit_message_wrap.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"scripts/check